  "question": {
    "text": "A car is moving along the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> in the anti-clockwise direction with a constant speed. The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></math> plane is a rough horizontal stationary surface. When the car is at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></math>,&nbsp;the unit vector in the direction of the friction force acting on the car is",
